  <!-- ========== TAB 2: ARCHITECTURE ========== -->
  <section class="tab-panel" id="architecture" role="tabpanel" data-tab-title="Architecture">
    <h2>How the Eval Benchmark Works</h2>

    <h3>Part 1: System Overview</h3>
    <p>The <code>ai-coding-rules</code> project maintains a versioned library of domain-specific coding rules encoded as Markdown files. These rules cover areas such as SQL conventions, Python style, security policy, deployment checklists, and Snowflake-specific patterns. The rules are not embedded in model weights&mdash;they live in a repository that teams control and update independently of any model release cycle. The protocol that governs how models consult these rules is defined in <code>AGENTS.md</code>, which is the entry point for the four-gate rule-loading sequence described in the Protocol tab.</p>

    <p>The eval benchmark exists to answer one operational question: <em>is the protocol being followed?</em> It sits alongside the rule library in the same repository and is invoked via the <code>ai-rules rule-loader eval</code> command exposed by the <strong>CoCo CLI</strong> (<code>cortex</code>). The CLI is the single interface through which fixture runs are dispatched, model connections are resolved, concurrency is controlled, and results are streamed to disk.</p>

